<title>AUSTRALIA: BHP says to shed 2,500 jobs at Newcastle.</title>
<headline>BHP says to shed 2,500 jobs at Newcastle.</headline>
<dateline>MELBOURNE 1997-04-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Australia's biggest company, The Broken Hill Pty Co Ltd (BHP), said on Tuesday it would shed up to 2,500 jobs with the closure of raw steel making at its Newcastle plant by the end of 1999.</p>
<p>The closure would leave about 400 to 500 workers operating the rod and bar mills on the site, BHP Newcastle spokesman Greg Cameron told Reuters.</p>
